## User Review Required

Please review the proposed architectural changes below. As per your strict instructions, **no code has been modified**. This is the blueprint for how the implementation will be executed once approved.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The frontend will request local images with query parameters like `?w=400&q=80` because of how `OptimizedImage.jsx` handles non-Cloudinary URLs. Nginx will ignore these query parameters and serve the full-resolution image. This means local images won't be dynamically resized on-the-fly like Cloudinary, but the images will still display perfectly without breaking the UI.

